      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Translumbar puncture for access to the central arterial tree has been used for aortography and for selective coronary angiography in selected patients where conventional peripheral access is not possible. A single case report of coronary angioplasty through this access technique is available in the literature. We report a case of coronary stent placement using the translumbar approach to access the coronary arteries."},
